   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 283 of the laws of 2023, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the town of Cornwall to impose a hotel and motel tax, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9107",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9107-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 283 of 2023",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9107\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 283 of the laws of 2023, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the town of Cornwall to impose a hotel and motel\ntax, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nExtends the authorization of the town of Cornwall in Orange County to\nimpose a hotel and motel tax.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 2 of chapter 283 of the laws of 2023, amending\nthe tax law relating to authorizing the town of Cornwall to impose a\nhotel and motel tax.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the town of Cornwall to continue to impose\na hotel and motel tax. The rate of such tax shall not exceed 5% of the\nper diem rental rate for each room. Pursuant to the Municipal Home Rule\nLaw, a town may adopt local laws that relate to the levy and adminis-\ntration of local taxes if authorized by the State legislature. The town\nof Cornwall has requested special legislation that will enable them to\ncontinue to collect a hotel and motel tax in an effort to raise addi-\ntional revenue for the town.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
